 outweigh Sununu's name recognition and the outside spending on his side, pointing to a clear but not safe Democratic edge in this open seat.", "watch": "Sustained Republican outside spending or a late national shift toward the GOP could tighten the polling gap and move this toward tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jeanne Shaheen (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's open Senate seat leans Democratic after Jeanne Shaheen's retirement. Chris Pappas has led in every independent poll since the September primaries, with margins between five and eight points, and published averages put him up around seven. Republican John Sununu, a former governor with deep name recognition, has kept Republican-aligned groups engaged, with outside spending favoring him by roughly three million dollars. Expert ratings split between Lean Democratic and Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price a Democratic win near ninety percent.\n\nPappas also holds a large fundraising advantage, having raised about four times Sununu's total, and the national environment appears favorable to Democrats. Sununu has worked to distance himself from Trump, and Democratic nervousness in local coverage suggests the race is not settled. The forecast expects Pappas to win by roughly seven points, with enough uncertainty that an upset remains possible.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8721, "margin": 5.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8221, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7959, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8661, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8028, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.837, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8746, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8609, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.856, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8659, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8767, "m